event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_083802ff2699d374016a1159d5896881918ecd5ee99ce08033","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":703,"text":"I can’t directly render an image in this chat, but I can give you a precise generation prompt that matches your request exactly.\n\n**Use this prompt:**\n\nCreate exactly **one** clean **HD 2D FX sprite sheet** arranged in a **2 rows by 3 columns** grid for a **cinematic game-start screen** in an **ocean-themed card game**. Use the provided image as **layout-only reference** for the sheet structure and frame arrangement, but **do not reproduce the guide lines, boxes, borders, or reference image content**.\n\n**Important requirements:**\n- **Background must be solid magenta `#FF00FF`** across the entire sprite sheet.\n- This is a **camera/lens opening effect**, **not** a card, UI panel, board, or scene illustration.\n- **No text** anywhere.\n- **No cards, hands, people, creatures, boards, ships, islands, or scene objects**.\n- Keep the **center readable and uncluttered** so the game can later render the title text in code.\n- Use a **full-screen cinematic look** with:\n  - soft iris bloom\n  - concentric lens rings\n  - subtle zoom pulse\n  - radiant light sweep\n  - watery refraction\n  - pearl glints\n  - faint radial rays\n- Keep all visible energy and highlights within the **central 70% safe area** of each frame.\n- Style: **clean HD 2D game FX**, polished, luminous, layered, smooth gradients, elegant and readable, no muddy details.\n\n**Frame sequence, left to right, top row then bottom row:**\n1. **Faint bloom** — very soft central glow, barely visible lens rings, gentle watery shimmer.\n2. **Opening ring** — iris-like concentric ring forms, slightly brighter bloom, subtle radial rays.\n3. **Stronger light sweep** — bright cinematic sweep crossing the center, more pronounced refraction and pearl glints.\n4. **Peak flash** — brightest frame, strong but controlled central flash, clean and not overfilled, center still readable.\n5. **Settling halo** — flash recedes into a refined halo with fading rings and soft oceanic shimmer.\n6. **Lingering afterglow** — dimmer residual bloom, faint lens rings, subtle watery refraction and tiny pearl glints.\n\n**Composition constraints:**\n- Each frame should feel like one step of the same opening effect.\n- Keep the effect centered and symmetrical overall, with slight natural variation in sweep and glints.\n- Avoid clutter near the exact center.\n- No frame numbers, labels, separators, or UI elements.\n- The final output should be **exactly one sprite sheet image**, not six separate images.\n\n**Visual palette:**\n- luminous whites\n- soft cyan\n- seafoam teal\n- pale aqua\n- cool pearl highlights\n\n**Negative prompt:**\ntext, letters, logo, title, cards, card backs, card faces, hands, people, faces, characters, board, table, ocean scene, horizon, ship, treasure, objects, interface, UI panel, frame borders, guide lines, reference layout, watermark, noise, gritty texture, cluttered center, asymmetrical off-center burst\n\nIf you want, I can also convert this into a **Midjourney**, **Stable Diffusion**, or **Photoshop/firefly-ready** version."}

